                    3, "The `await` keyword suspends the current coroutine, yielding control back to the asyncio event loop so other tasks can run while waiting for an I/O operation. Believing it blocks the OS thread defeats the entire purpose of async concurrency. Mastering the event loop is crucial for high-performance Python backends.",
