                    new[] { "They are completely interchangeable syntaxes for the same operation.", "`try` requires a do-catch block, `try?` converts an error to a `nil` optional, and `try!` crashes the app if an error occurs.", "`try` handles synchronous errors, `try?` handles async errors, and `try!` ignores errors completely.", "`try` is for network requests, `try?` is for database calls, and `try!` is for UI updates." },
                    1, "`try?` gracefully swallows the error into a `nil` optional, `try!` forcibly assumes success (crashing on error), and `try` forces you to handle the error explicitly. Using `try!` carelessly guarantees production crashes. Mastering this syntax enables robust error handling.",
                    skillId: 10),
                CreateQuestion(id++, "What do the higher-order functions `map`, `filter`, and `reduce` do to a collection?",
