                    new[] { "`main` is used for high-priority background tasks, while `global()` handles user input.", "`main` executes strictly on the server, while `global()` executes on the local device.", "`main` allows multiple threads simultaneously, while `global()` is strictly single-threaded.", "`main` is a serial queue reserved for UI updates, while `global()` returns concurrent background queues for heavy processing." },
                    3, "`DispatchQueue.main` handles UI and runs on the single main thread; `global()` provides background threads for heavy lifting. Blocking the main queue freezes the app. Dispatching heavy work to `global` and UI updates back to `main` is the golden rule of iOS performance.",
